stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Authenticating: Read vendor meetings
    Authenticating --> Reading: Partner or verified local wrapper reads its partner calendar
    Authenticating --> Refused: Caller has no mailbox authority or selects a sponsor
    Refused: Refuse before database reads
    Refused --> [*]
    Reading --> SourceUnavailable: Calendar read fails or source is missing
    Reading --> InvalidDurationUnavailable: A displayed meeting has no duration
    Reading --> SourceUnavailable: Coverage is stale, future, malformed, or truncated
    Reading --> CoveredReady: Fresh coverage has gaps of at least thirty minutes
    Reading --> CoveredEmpty: Fresh coverage has no qualifying gaps
    Reading --> WarningPartial: Known warnings and qualifying gaps
    SourceUnavailable: Scheduling unavailable, no candidate gaps
    InvalidDurationUnavailable: Scheduling unavailable, agenda stays visible
    CoveredReady: Show candidate gaps, confirm in Outlook
    CoveredEmpty: No candidate gaps
    WarningPartial: Show candidate gaps with uncertainty
    SourceUnavailable --> [*]
    InvalidDurationUnavailable --> [*]
    CoveredReady --> [*]
    CoveredEmpty --> [*]
    WarningPartial --> [*]
    %% never Offer candidate gaps when a displayed meeting has zero duration.
    %% never Rewrite a missing or delayed source as an empty calendar.
    %% The awaited database read settles before projection. No owned background work or teardown.

    [*] --> ProofReading: Observe release and authenticated calendar
    ProofReading --> ProofInsufficient: Read fails, deadline expires, or response exceeds one MiB
    ProofReading --> ProofInsufficient: Natural evidence is absent or release changes
    ProofReading --> ProofPassed: Natural zero-duration row has no candidate gaps
    ProofReading --> ProofContradiction: Natural zero-duration row still has candidate gaps
    ProofInsufficient: Insufficient observation, exit 78
    ProofPassed: Both assertions pass, exit 0
    ProofContradiction: Contradiction, exit 1
    ProofInsufficient --> [*]: Kill owned wrapper group and reap leader
    ProofPassed --> [*]: Kill owned wrapper group and reap leader
    ProofContradiction --> [*]: Kill owned wrapper group and reap leader
    %% never Drain wrapper stdout beyond one MiB plus one overflow byte.
    %% never Let caller input choose a calendar owner or turn an agent into a human.
